      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Labor pain management has changed dramatically during the last 20 years, and recently the nurse's role with epidural analgesia and anesthesia has been called into question. Cost-cutting measures in hospitals and clinics have forced some RNs into roles typically, and advisedly, reserved for a certified anesthesia provider--sometimes to the mother and baby's peril."},
